Change Date,Rulebook,Effective Date,Rule Module,Former Rule,,Latter Rule,Reason
6/12/2026,A,6/12/2026,Module B,Entry signal: Price pulls back to the 20-day Moving Average in an uptrend,->,Entry Signal: Price within 2% of the 20-day MA,Clarified breakout definition
6/12/2026,A,6/12/2026,Module A,Entry Signal: price closes above the 20 day high,->,Entry Signal: price closes above the prior 20 day high,Removed subjective interpretation
6/12/2026,A,6/12/2026,Module B,Entry Signal: Price within 2% of the 20-day MA,->,Price within 1.5 x ATR(14) of the 20 day MA,replaced fixed percentage threshold with volatility-adjusted threshold using ATR(14)
6/16/2026,A,6/16/2026,Module B,Volume > 30?day Average Volume,->,Volume < 30?day Average Volume,"Pullbacks occur on declining volume as selling pressure dries up. High volume during a pullback indicates institutional distribution, which invalidates a long setup. This change aligns volume behavior with the intended pullback structure."
6/16/2026,A,6/16/2026,Market Filters,"S&P 500 > 200MA
50% of stocks > 200MA
VIX < 25",->,50% of S&P 500 stocks > 200MA,Keeping all three creates redundant constraints that block valid setups during early market recoveries. Market breadth is the most robust and predictive of the three.
6/16/2026,A,6/16/2026,Module A,Enter at next day’s open,->,Enter at prior day’s close OR at 2:55 PM CST,"Breakouts frequently gap up the next morning, causing poor entry prices and breaking the 2 × ATR risk model. Entering at the close eliminates slippage and preserves the intended risk?reward structure."
6/16/2026,A,6/16/2026,Module B,Price within 1.5 × ATR(14) of 20MA,->,Price within 2.0 × ATR(14) of 20MA,1.5 × ATR creates an unrealistically narrow pullback zone that excludes most healthy trends. Expanding the envelope allows participation in normal volatility while maintaining structure.
7/3/2026,B,,Module B,Price consolidates tightly within the Keltner bands for 3+ days AND Price pierces and closes above the upper Keltner Channel,->,Prior Condition: Price consolidated tightly inside the Keltner bands for the prior 3+ trading days.                                             Entry Signal: Price pierces and closes above the 20-day EMA line.,Resolved a mathematical logic lock. A stock cannot physically be tightly inside a channel and piercing outside of it simultaneously on a low-volume close. Splitting it into a chronological sequence allows the strategy to execute.
7/3/2026,B,,Module B,Price pierces and closes above the 20-day EMA line.(Loosely executed in code version 1 as a general state check: Price > 20-day EMA),->,Prior Condition: Price consolidated tightly inside the Keltner bands for the prior 3+ trading days.Entry Signal: Price pierces and closes above the 20-day EMA line.,"Realigned code with strict text definitions. Forcing a rigid single-day cross-under condition triggered a heavy overfitting penalty. Total return collapsed from 37.99% to 20.10% because the rigid parameter blocked participation in rolling support bounces, proving that flexible trend rules outperform hyper-optimized timing windows."
7/3/2026,"A, B, C",,Execution Infra,Enter at 2:55 PM CST or prior day's close.,->,Execution via Market-On-Close (MOC) routing protocol based on 2:50 PM projected signals.,Standardizes live automation syntax. Resolves the data-fetching time lock by utilizing institutional order types that guarantee execution at the 3:00 PM CST closing cross print.
7/5/2026,"A, B, C",,Execution Engine / Timing,Enter at prior day's close OR at 3:00 PM CST / 2:55 PM CST.,->,Next-Day Opening-Bell Execution: Signals lock at daily close; trades execute at next morning's opening bell print.,Eliminates look-ahead bias and intraday time-travel execution anomalies.
7/5/2026,"A, B, C",,Risk Rules / Portfolio Capacity,Maximum 6 positions open at once / One single trade cannot have more than 1/6 of portfolio.,->,"Dynamic Decrement Loop: Position size capped at 1/6 ($16,666) of total equity, calculated using true next-day opening print plus friction fees.",Prevents overnight gaps from breaking the 1% equity risk ceiling and hard-enforces capital bounds.
7/5/2026,C,,Entry / Logic Hierarchy,Entry Module A (RSI < 10) and Entry Module B (RSI < 5) evaluated independently.,->,Hierarchical Clear: Deep pullback signal (RSI < 5) overrides standard entry to prevent duplicate tickers.,Re-architects overlapping conditional statements into explicit if/elif chains to kill asset duplication.
7/5/2026,"A, B, C",,Risk Rules / Capacity Synchronization,Entry and exits evaluated simultaneously at market close.,->,Sequential Accounting Gate: Exits are permanently calculated and portfolio capacity resets on morning exits before new entries scan.,Synchronizes available cash ledger balances and slot counters to prevent capital allocation overlap.
7/5/2026,B,,Data Sourcing / Time Offset,Squeeze criteria checked on current day data arrays.,->,Static Array Pinning: Index tracking pinned strictly to iloc[-1] based on yesterday's completed daily close.,Ensures complete insulation against streaming or un-settled data leakage during afternoon scans.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Market Regime Filter,Market_OK = SPX > 200-SMA,->,Market_OK = (SPX > 200-SMA) AND (SPX > 50-SMA),200-SMA alone is too slow; prevents entries during early crash phases.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Yin Volatility Breaker,Yin enters solely based on RSI2 thresholds.,->,Yin blocks entries when ATR14 > 2 × ATR50.,Prevents catastrophic mean-reversion traps during volatility explosions.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Allocation Ordering,Ticker loop executed alphabetically (MSFT ? TSLA).,->,All signals ranked by strength; strongest signals allocated first.,Removes alphabetical bias; ensures fair capital allocation.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Sector Cap Enforcement,Sector caps checked only before candidate generation.,->,Sector caps enforced inside ranked execution loop.,Prevents over-allocation when multiple high-strength signals occur in same sector.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Signal Strength Computation,No ranking; signals treated equally.,->,Strength = (distance beyond breakout) / ATR or (10 ? RSI2) for Yin.,Normalizes signal quality; improves trade selection.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Unified Entry Pipeline,Entry logic executed inline inside ticker loop.,->,"Entry logic split into: 1) Candidate discovery, 2) Strength scoring, 3) Ranked allocation with sector caps",Cleaner architecture; prevents race conditions and improves consistency.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Regime Filter Messaging,“PASS” based only on 200-SMA.,->,“PASS” requires both 200-SMA and 50-SMA.,Aligns printed output with new regime logic; prevents misleading signals.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Yin Time-Stop Safety,Yin exits only after 4 days or SMA5 breach.,->,Yin also blocks entries during volatility spikes (ATR breaker).,Reduces probability of forced exits at worst possible moment.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Zhan Consolidation Logic,Consolidation checked inside alphabetical loop.,->,Consolidation checked during candidate generation; ranked afterward.,Ensures consolidation signals are evaluated before ranking; improves accuracy.
7/6/2026,Forward Test Engine,7/6/2026,Entry Cost Validation,Entry cost validated only after alphabetical loop.,->,Entry cost validated inside ranked loop with sector caps.,Prevents invalid entries when ranking changes order of evaluation.
7/7/2026,Version 2.6 (Live Desk),7/7/2026,State Tracking & Memory,New position dictionary keys stored only sector and shares leaving background variables out.,->,State Retention Update: New position dictionaries initialize with sector shares stop and days_held: 0 explicitly on entry.,Restoring the background keys prevents the engine from hitting a fatal KeyError and crashing the next afternoon when checking for active trade exits.
7/7/2026,B (Zhan),7/7/2026,Volatility Squeeze Lookback,Squeeze evaluation used range(2-5) which completely skipped today's current asset close.,->,Lookback Realignment: Squeeze criteria index window shifted back to range(1-4).,Forces the engine to check today's completed closing data alongside the prior two days ensuring recent breakouts successfully qualify.
7/7/2026,C (Yin),7/7/2026,Priority Signal Allocation,Evaluated signal tiers inside a flat loop where deep and standard panic pullbacks got identical priority scores.,->,Hierarchical Split: Re-architected signals into clean if/elif branches where an RSI under 5 scores a higher priority than an RSI under 10.,Guarantees that deep exhaustion setups are mathematically prioritized at the top of the queue when portfolio capacity slots are limited.
7/7/2026,Version 2.6 (Live Desk),7/7/2026,Ledger Automation,Active open positions had to have their duration integers incremented by hand every afternoon.,->,Automated Ledger Increment: Added an automatic for loop that increments days_held by 1 for all existing positions at startup.,Completely removes human manual-entry math errors during the 13-month forward testing routine.
7/7/2026,Execution Logic,7/8/2026,Yang Module B Strength,(sma50 - close_spot) / atr14,(close_spot - sma50) / atr14,Correct formula inversion bug to properly prioritize top momentum leaders rather than assets nearing trend breakdown.,
7/10/2026,"Models A, B, C",7/10/2026,Data Ingestion Base,Historical calculations pulled using default unadjusted pricing structures.,,Historical data locked strictly to dividend and stock-split adjusted closing values.,Data Continuity: Prevents massive false indicators on names like NVDA and TSLA that underwent major stock splits.
7/10/2026,Model A (Yang),7/10/2026,High-Volume Breakout,Discovered 20-day high breakouts using current daily candle data in the loop.,,Entry signals evaluated strictly using the prior day's fully finalized 20-day high.,Eliminated Look-Ahead Bias: Prevents the system from seeing today's close before trading today's open.
7/10/2026,"Models A, B, C",7/10/2026,Trade Fill Execution,All positions assumed filled precisely at historical stop-loss target regardless of gaps.,,"Positions filled at stop-loss target unless stock gaps below stop price, then filled at worse open price.",Fixed Execution Logic: Models real-world risk and prevents artificial optimization during market panics.
7/10/2026,"Models A, B, C",7/10/2026,Multi-Signal Sizing,Capital allocated to multiple simultaneous morning signals using unrestricted static cash balance.,,Available equity dynamically reduced after each individual candidate is processed.,Capital Protection: Stops the engine from buying too many shares when multiple setups fire on the same morning.
7/10/2026,Model C (Yin),7/10/2026,Re-entry Churn Gate,Assets allowed to immediately re-trigger a buy signal on the same day they were sold.,,Stocks exited at 3:00 PM CST are barred from re-entering until the next trading session.,Whipsaw Prevention: Improves win rate by stopping the engine from chasing a tanking stock.
7/10/2026,Model C (Yin),7/10/2026,Volatility Breaker,RSI exhaustion setups evaluated regardless of total market volatility conditions.,,Entries blocked when short-term volatility (14-day ATR) is double long-term volatility (50-day ATR).,Tail-Risk Filter: Avoids dangerous falling knife situations where mean reversion fails.
7/10/2026,Model B (Zhan),7/10/2026,Breakout Validation,Breakout entries triggered immediately upon crossing Keltner Channel band.,,Requires stock to close inside upper and lower channel boundaries for 3 consecutive days before entry.,Squeeze Verification: Confirms true asset compression before risking capital on breakout.
7/10/2026,"Models A, B, C",7/10/2026,Portfolio Tracking,Portfolio net worth calculated using cash accounts and closed trade cycles only.,,Active open positions revalued daily using current mark-to-market closing data.,Drawdown Transparency: Reveals true maximum drawdown and active risk exposure during market swings.
7/10/2026,Metrics Engine,7/10/2026,Performance Scoring,Sharpe and Sortino ratios calculated using a baseline 0% risk-free rate only.,,Strategy returns benchmarked against an annualized 4.5% modern yield curve.,Institutional Standards: Forces strategy to prove it can outperform high-yield cash accounts on a risk-adjusted basis.
7/10/2026,"Models A, B, C",7/10/2026,Transaction Friction,Backtests performed under frictionless zero-fee execution assumptions.,,Applies 5 basis points (0.05%) slippage per entry/exit and $1.00 flat fee per trade.,Friction Penalization: Ensures high-turnover models like Yin's 835 trades remain profitable under realistic conditions.
